@node Binary Search Trees Types
@section Types
@cindex binary search trees, types

@deftp {Data Type} {gsl_bst_type}
A structure containing the function pointers and other properties that
define one kind of tree.  The library provides two instances,
@code{gsl_bst_avl} and @code{gsl_bst_rb}; the routines below take one of
these as their @var{T} argument.
@end deftp

@deftp {Data Type} {gsl_bst_cmp_function}
The type of the comparison function:

@example
int compare (const void * a, const void * b, void * params);
@end example

@noindent
It must return a negative value if @var{a} orders before @var{b}, zero if
the two are equal, and a positive value otherwise.
@end deftp

@deftp {Data Type} {gsl_bst_allocator}
A replacement memory allocator:

@example
typedef struct
@{
  void * (*alloc) (size_t size, void * params);
  void (*free) (void * block, void * params);
@} gsl_bst_allocator;
@end example

@noindent
A null pointer passed to @code{gsl_bst_alloc} selects the standard
@code{malloc} and @code{free} functions.
@end deftp

@deftp {Data Type} {gsl_bst_workspace}
A workspace holding a tree and its associated state.  It is created by
@code{gsl_bst_alloc} and released with @code{gsl_bst_free}.
@end deftp

@deftp {Data Type} {gsl_bst_trav}
A traverser, used to walk through a tree in order.
@end deftp

@node Binary Search Trees Allocation
@section Allocation

@deftypefun {gsl_bst_workspace *} gsl_bst_alloc (const gsl_bst_type * @var{T}, const gsl_bst_allocator * @var{allocator}, gsl_bst_cmp_function * @var{compare}, void * @var{params})
This function allocates and initializes a tree of type @var{T}, which
must be @code{gsl_bst_avl} or @code{gsl_bst_rb}.  The @var{compare}
function defines the ordering, and @var{params} is passed unchanged to it
and to the allocator.  On success the new workspace is returned; on
failure a null pointer is returned and the error handler is invoked with
@code{GSL_ENOMEM}.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void gsl_bst_free (gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function frees every node in @var{w} and the workspace itself.  The
items stored in the tree are not freed; if the tree owns them, the caller
must free them first.
@end deftypefun

@node Binary Search Trees Modifying
@section Modifying the tree

@deftypefun int gsl_bst_empty (gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function removes every item from @var{w}, leaving it empty.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_insert (void * @var{item}, gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function inserts @var{item} into the tree.  If an equal item is
already present, no insertion takes place and a pointer to the existing
item is returned; otherwise @var{item} is stored and returned.  A null
pointer is returned if memory for the new node cannot be obtained.  The
library stores the pointer it is given and does not copy the item, so the
item must stay valid while it is in the tree.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_find (const void * @var{item}, const gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function returns a pointer to the item in the tree equal to
@var{item}, or a null pointer if there is none.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_remove (const void * @var{item}, gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function removes the item equal to @var{item} and returns a pointer
to it.  If no matching item is present the tree is unchanged and a null
pointer is returned.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun size_t gsl_bst_nodes (const gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function returns the number of items in the tree.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun size_t gsl_bst_node_size (const gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function returns the size in bytes of each node.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun {const char *} gsl_bst_name (const gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function returns a string naming the tree type, such as
@code{"AVL"} or @code{"RB"}.
@end deftypefun

@node Binary Search Trees Traversal
@section Traversal

A traverser walks the items of a tree in their sorted order.  It must be
initialized by @code{gsl_bst_trav_first}, @code{gsl_bst_trav_last},
@code{gsl_bst_trav_find} or @code{gsl_bst_trav_init} before use, and it
is invalidated by any modification of the tree.

@deftypefun int gsl_bst_trav_init (gsl_bst_trav * @var{trav}, const gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function initializes @var{trav} for the tree @var{w}.  The traverser
is not positioned on any item.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_trav_first (gsl_bst_trav * @var{trav}, const gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function initializes @var{trav} and returns the least-valued item in
the tree, or a null pointer if the tree is empty.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_trav_last (gsl_bst_trav * @var{trav}, const gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function initializes @var{trav} and returns the greatest-valued item
in the tree, or a null pointer if the tree is empty.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_trav_find (const void * @var{item}, gsl_bst_trav * @var{trav}, const gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function searches for @var{item}, positions @var{trav} on it and
returns it, or returns a null pointer if the item is not present.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_trav_insert (void * @var{item}, gsl_bst_trav * @var{trav}, gsl_bst_workspace * @var{w})
This function behaves as @code{gsl_bst_insert}, but also positions
@var{trav} on the inserted item (or on the existing duplicate).
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_trav_copy (gsl_bst_trav * @var{dest}, const gsl_bst_trav * @var{src})
This function copies the traverser @var{src} into @var{dest} and returns
a pointer to the current item.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_trav_next (gsl_bst_trav * @var{trav})
This function advances @var{trav} to the next item in order and returns
it, or returns a null pointer if there is none.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_trav_prev (gsl_bst_trav * @var{trav})
This function moves @var{trav} to the previous item in order and returns
it, or returns a null pointer if there is none.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_trav_cur (const gsl_bst_trav * @var{trav})
This function returns the current item without moving the traverser.
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun void * gsl_bst_trav_replace (gsl_bst_trav * @var{trav}, void * @var{new_item})
This function replaces the current item with @var{new_item} and returns
the item it replaced.  The replacement must compare equal to the item it
replaces, so that the ordering of the tree is unchanged.
@end deftypefun

